# Anchor ignore patterns to the repository root on purpose: a bare `build/`
# (Gradle-era) matched at *any* depth and silently excluded five vendored
# proto files whose upstream paths contain a `build` component — including
# build_event_stream.proto, the entire BEP schema. Prefer a pattern that lets
# a stray directory show up noisily in `git status` over one that can quietly
# drop source files.

/out/
bin/

# Bazel outputs and convenience symlinks. Anchored to the repository root for
# the same reason the build/ patterns above are anchored: a bare `bazel-*`
# matches at any depth and would swallow the tracked `bazel-runner/`
# compatibility package (its source moved to `runner/` in ADR-010). Several
# vendored proto paths contain "bazel" too. The last entry is the workspace
# symlink Bazel names after the repository directory.
/bazel-bin
/bazel-out
/bazel-testlogs
/bazel-bazel-bep-viewer

# jpackage output from `bazel run //app:jpackage` (see docs/packaging.md).
/dist/

.DS_Store
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/

# JetBrains' Bazel plugin materializes its downloaded/generated BSP aspects
# here. They are machine-local cache state, not part of the repository.
/.bazelbsp/

# Codex keeps isolated Git worktrees below this root. Committing one would add
# a gitlink whose branch and lifetime belong to a separate task.
/.Codex/

hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# Claude Code's per-session state, including the git worktrees it creates for
# isolated work. A worktree under here is a checkout of this same repository,
# so committing one adds a gitlink that clones cannot resolve — and it captures
# whatever branch someone else happens to have in progress.
.claude/
